<item><title>Sierra Leone charcoal trade sustains families as tree cutting threatens forests</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-charcoal-trade-sustains-families-as-tree-a237a3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-charcoal-trade-sustains-families-as-tree-a237a3/</guid><category>Sierra Leone</category><description>A 65-year-old burner says his family relies on the work, while the environment agency warns that producers are cutting orange and mango trees.</description><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:12:17 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" length="34790" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Sierra Leone regulator reports NLE 7.4 million in 2024 revenue</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-regulator-reports-nle-7-4-million-in-2024-333409/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-regulator-reports-nle-7-4-million-in-2024-333409/</guid><category>Sierra Leone</category><description>The electricity and water regulator said levies and licenses generated more than the NLE 2.3 million recorded in 2023.</description><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:12:17 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-regulator-reports-nle-7-4-million-in-2024-333409/share.jpg" length="41494" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-regulator-reports-nle-7-4-million-in-2024-333409/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Sierra Leone’s vice presidency has produced no elected successor</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-s-vice-presidency-has-produced-no-elected-b42fab/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-s-vice-presidency-has-produced-no-elected-b42fab/</guid><category>Sierra Leone</category><description>A political analyst says the office has often balanced party blocs rather than prepared vice presidents to lead, citing Solomon Berewa’s 2007 defeat.</description><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:12:16 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" length="34790" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
